what:
One added entry in crates/hir-ty/src/mir/held.rs for lane may-suspend (docs/v2/plan/lanes/may-suspend.md, 'The check'): the same analyses as `MirBody::held_locals_in`, with the suspend points given instead of the body's `Yield`s.

    /// The locals held across the call that ends each block of `points`, as `held_locals_in`
    /// finds them across a yield: live after the call (`MaybeLiveLocals`, the call's own
    /// destination not), or borrowed before it (`MaybeBorrowedLocals`), while their storage is
    /// required (`MaybeRequiresStorage`, after the call's whole moves of its operands). The first
    /// parameter is an ordinary one here (not removed as a coroutine's receiver is); promoted
    /// constants are removed as there. One slice per point, in order, each in the order the
    /// body declares its locals; an unreached block's is empty.
    pub fn held_across_calls_in<'f>(&self, frame: &'f Frame, points: &[BasicBlockId]) -> &'f [&'f [LocalId]]

Sketch: `reachable`, `forward`, `liveness` once; per point: `forward.load`, `storage_statement` over the block's statements, then `kill_whole_move` over the terminator's operands and `requires.remove(destination.local)`; `live = live_out[block] ∪ borrowed ∩ requires`, minus `promoted_constants`. Everything in `frame`.
Why: hir-ty-suspend (new) rejects a `!Send` or `#[must_not_suspend]` value held across a call that may park a fiber; Andrew asked that liveness be exactly the analysis rustc runs for values held across `.await`, which is this file. Tell lane may-suspend (window may-suspend) when done.
